{title: We Plow the Fields and Scatter}
{artist: Matthias Claudius · tr. Jane Campbell}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
We [Bb]plow the fields and [Eb]scatter the [F]good seed on the [Bb]land,
but it is fed and [Eb]watered by [F]God's almighty [Bb]hand:
he [F]sends the snow in [Bb]winter, the [F]warmth to swell the [Gm]grain,
the [Bb]breezes and the [Eb]sunshine, and [F]soft refreshing [Bb]rain.

Chorus
All good gifts a[Eb]round us are [F]sent from heaven a[Bb]bove —
then thank the Lord, O [Eb]thank the Lord for [F]all his [Bb]love.
